    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gary_Numan> ;
    riff:describes influence:gary_numan--brian_eno ;
    riff:evidenceQuote "Moving away from the commercially successful synth-pop on the 1979 studio albums Replicas and The Pleasure Principle to a more introspective and partly ambient sound, David Bowie's collaborations with Brian Eno, the new wave band Japan and Lou Reed's third solo studio album Berlin (1973) has been cited as some of the influences that informed Numan's third solo studio album Dance (1981)."@en ;
    riff:hasEvidenceKind riff:Attributed .

claim:gary_numan--depeche_mode--attributed a riff:InfluenceClaim ;
