    riff:describes influence:patti_smith--the_byrds ;
    riff:evidenceQuote "\"So You Want to Be a Rock 'n' Roll Star\" was issued as a single in January 1967 and peaked at number 29 in America but failed to chart in the UK. Despite this relatively poor chart showing, \"So You Want to Be a Rock 'n' Roll Star\" has become one of the Byrds' best-known songs in the years since its initial release, inspiring cover versions by the likes of Tom Petty and the Heartbreakers and the Patti Smith Group among others."@en ;
